From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Tue, 11 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: use duelist helpers in card, effect, duel, playerop and
 API code

Phase 1 site work for card.cpp, effect.cpp, duel.cpp, playerop.cpp and ocgapi.cpp. No behaviour change with 2 duelists.

Changed:
- 13 "1 - x" sites now use opponent_of (12 in card.cpp, 1 in playerop.cpp). In card.cpp x is the controler of a card on the field (0 or 1), or a summon player that goes into a uint8_t. In playerop.cpp x already indexes hint_timing[2].
- 1 loop over duelists uses n_duelists as bound (ocgapi.cpp OCG_DuelQueryField). card.cpp get_unique_target keeps its stock bound: it is a relative self/opponent loop over unique_pos[2].
- 1 turn-player-first loop (playerop.cpp counter select) counts n_duelists steps and uses next_in_turn_order.
- 4 validity checks use is_duelist (ocgapi.cpp 3, playerop.cpp 1). All take a uint8_t, so the accept set is 0 and 1 with 2 duelists.

Why it is the same: opponent_of(x) equals 1 - x for x in 0..1, n_duelists is 2, next_in_turn_order(p) equals 1 - p for 2 duelists, and is_duelist accepts exactly 0 and 1.

Left unchanged: PLAYER_NONE checks, absolute target tests (player 0 or 1), the Rock Paper Scissors win code, SIMPLE_AI player 1 tests, member array pairs owned by agent H, and Domain anchor text. effect.cpp, duel.cpp, interpreter.cpp, processor_visit.cpp and scriptlib.cpp have no changed site. See unchanged-sites.md.
